{"name":"Grey Suit","hex":"#807a77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"suit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of clothes to be worn together, now especially a man's matching jacket and trousers (also business suit or lounge suit), or a similar outfit for a woman.","A garment or set of garments suitable and/or required for a given task or activity: space suit, boiler suit, protective suit, swimsuit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make proper or suitable; to adapt or fit.","To be suitable or apt for one's image."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grey Suit","blocks":[{"text":"Grey Suit is the second extended play by South Korean singer Suho. It was released on April 4, 2022, by SM Entertainment. The EP contains six tracks including the lead single of the same name. The physical album is available in three versions two photobook versions and one digipack version"}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/47/Suho_-_Grey_Suit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_Suit","wikidata":"Q111620817"},{"title":"Suit","blocks":[{"text":"A suit, also called a lounge suit, business suit, dress suit, or formal suit, is a set of clothes comprising a suit jacket and trousers of identical textiles generally worn with a collared dress shirt, necktie, and dress shoes. A skirt suit is similar, but with a matching pencil skirt instead of trousers. It is currently considered semi-formal wear or business wear in contemporary Western dress codes; however, when the suit was originally developed it was considered an informal or more casual option compared to the prevailing clothing standards of aristocrats and businessmen. The lounge suit originated in 19th-century Britain as sportswear and British country clothing, which is why it was seen as more casual than citywear at that time, with the roots of the suit coming from early modern Western Europe formal court or military clothes. After replacing the black frock coat in the early 20th century as regular daywear, a sober one-coloured suit became known as a lounge suit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Matt_Smith_on_%22Christopher_And_His_Kind%22_set.jpg/330px-Matt_Smith_on_%22Christopher_And_His_Kind%22_set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit","wikidata":"Q614806"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Gentleman_in_bowler.JPG/330px-Gentleman_in_bowler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Gentleman_in_bowler.JPG/330px-Gentleman_in_bowler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man dressed in a three-piece suit and bowler hat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGentleman_in_bowler.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Three_Piece_%28SBW%29_Tweed_%E2%80%93_Yellow-Oli